WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.802
A small Texas town divided at odds over

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.037
what Elon Musk and SpaceX

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.139
X have done to their peaceful livelihoods

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.341
as they sit in the shadow of behemoths.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.976
SpaceX facilities

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.044
On the flip side,

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.313
it's also brought an economic boom.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:16.850
Ed Lavandera is OUTFRONT

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.651
Looks like the surface of the moon.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.221
Yeah, it looks otherworldly.

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.289
Take a walk through the sand dunes

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.657
surrounding the SpaceX

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.860
launch pad tower in south Texas.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.294
And the remnants of April's

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:28.862
launch

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.363
of the most powerful rocket

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.432
ever built are still everywhere.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.333
These pieces right here

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.568
were part of the launch pad. Yeah. Wow.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.737
And this is only a quarter of a mile.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.938
Maybe debris

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.307
that size went three quarters of a mile.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.310
At least after the launch just in LA,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.346
Claire documented the aftermath.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.447
He's a biologist

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.915
with the Coastal Bend Bays

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.517
and Estuaries Program,

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.151
a group

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.253
that's tracking the environmental impact

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:53.987
of space

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.356
launches on the Boca Chica Peninsula.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.258
The area is now often

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:01.261
referred to as Elon Musk's Starbase.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.629
It is in the middle of a wildlife

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:03.997
refuge and state park lands.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.132
And, you know,

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:06.766
this this

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.802
area isn't really meant to be disturbed.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.770
That's kind of the point of protecting

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.704
these areas,

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.006
is to protect them

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:13.573
for the wildlife

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:16.142
and for public enjoyment as well.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.446
In April, thousands of people descended

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.480
on South Texas

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.915
to witness the thunderous

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.416
launch of the SpaceX

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.752
Starship Rocket and heavy booster

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.123
The rocket's three engines

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.492
disintegrated much of the concrete

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.560
launch pad.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.295
And then a few minutes later,

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.563
the rocket blew up

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.298
before reaching SpaceX,

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.532
literally like a meteor.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.668
Debris from the launch left craters

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:42.836
in the sand flats.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:45.138
Smaller pieces peppered the landscape

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.574
like a shotgun blast at close range.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.676
Tangled rebar was thrown nearly

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.944
a mile away.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.246
Vegetation near the site was scorched.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.748
The area is a critical nesting ground

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.051
for threatened and endangered wildlife.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.119
What is your concern

00:01:59.119 --> 00:01:59.853
about what this place

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.587
is going to look like?

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.321
Yeah, well,

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.822
that's the that's the question is

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.057
where does it stop, really?

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.225
Another explosion another explosion.

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:07.427
Another explosion eventually.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:08.228
Like this

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:11.064
is not a wildlife refuge anymore.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.465
It's not a place for the public

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.434
to go and see natural beauty.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.836
It's for space testing and space travel.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:17.570
And that's it.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.539
The April launch has resurfaced,

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:20.140
the tension

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.908
between Elon Musk's SpaceX

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:24.210
and its critics here in South Texas.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.813
This graffiti appeared just a week later.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.415
Several environmental groups are suing

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.417
the Federal Aviation Administration

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.253
to take stricter oversight

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:34.854
of the private space company's

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.122
launch plans.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.724
SpaceX did not respond

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.626
to CNN's requests for comment.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:40.593
It's not clear

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.428
when SpaceX will launch again.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.130
Elon Musk says he'd like to try

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.499
by the end of July or early August.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.934
But the Federal Aviation

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.702
Administration tells CNN

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.105
that it will not speculate on a timeline

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.007
to approve future flights.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.176
The FAA says that SpaceX has yet

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:57.010
to complete

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.245
its final mishap investigation

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.513
and that the company still needs

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.381
to identify

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.282
and implement

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.416
corrective actions

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.251
to ensure public safety.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.287
A lot of it is space themed.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:09.055
Barton Bickerton opened Hopper

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:11.291
House Bar and Grill almost two years ago.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.259
It's become a popular spot

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.928
for space sex employees,

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.030
locals and space tourists.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.965
Business has been booming.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:19.966
We had a lot of regulars

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:20.967
that were coming in every day

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.702
and really supportive of it,

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.370
and now we're kind of you know,

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.241
again, they were just kind of shocked

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:29.609
by it.

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.044
So, like, more nervous about what

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.779
the impact and all that might be.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.247
There's no turning back from this now,

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:34.514
right?

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:35.114
There's no way

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:35.582
that they're not

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.116
going to keep launching from here.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.618
These guys will figure it out.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:38.918
You know,

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.620
they'll figure out what they need to do.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.689
The space boom has also triggered

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.457
a real estate boom.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.658
This is old Brownsville

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:46.993
but this is old Brownsville.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.528
You grew up a few blocks.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.295
I grew up

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:52.131
two blocks down that way on Levy.

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.935
So, yeah, I it's home.

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.303
Josette Hinojosa

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.038
isn't sure how much longer

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.040
she can afford to live here.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.710
She says her rent jumped from $650

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:06.746
a month to a thousand in just two years.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.281
Hinojosa says

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.283
many families are selling their homes

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.584
because they can't afford

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.919
the taxes anymore.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:15.521
That is my fear for my neighbors.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.157
That they will be shut out.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:18.925
They will be pushed

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.260
out of the neighborhood

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.328
and the place that we know is home.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.263
Brownsville is in

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.298
one of the poorest counties in the state.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:26.399
But the median home

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.368
price has more than doubled

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:31.738
since space broke ground here in 2014,

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.373
far outpacing

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:35.141
the statewide price increase

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:35.942
It's like this

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.344
polarizing issue within our city

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.713
because you have people who work for them

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:41.814
and then you've got

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:42.582
people like me

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:43.049
who are like,

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:43.850
you guys are

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.551
looking at the bigger picture

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.019
Space

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.787
X has the full throttle support

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.355
of local political leaders

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.191
who see space as a major economic driver

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.993
that will fundamentally change

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:56.095
the future of the Rio Grande Valley.

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.698
The company is expanding its footprint

00:04:58.698 --> 00:04:59.599
on the South Texas

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:00.333
coast,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.502
and Elon Musk has committed millions

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.536
to the community.

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:04.971
We're inventing the wheel

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.506
with the largest

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:08.775
potential spaceship that's ever been

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.476
launched or developed.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.645
Cameron County Judge Eddie Trevino says.

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:14.747
It's like the early days of Nasser

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:15.948
when the space agency

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.950
developed Cape Canaveral, Florida.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.052
I guarantee you

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.186
any other community

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.120
in this country

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.455
would love to have Space X

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.990
launching in their backyard

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.124
because of what it would mean

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.793
from an economic development standpoint,

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.761
from an educational standpoint,

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.397
from a tourism standpoint.

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:33.800
Ed Lavandera, CNN, Brownsville, Texas.

